{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b579f2dc-602a-4471-816a-fd61e87e6a93",
    "name": "Distributed E-Commerce Order Management System",
    "description": "API collection for the MS Computer Science capstone project - Product, Order, Inventory, and Notification services, fronted by the Spring Cloud Gateway and secured with Keycloak OAuth2/OIDC.\n\n## Before you start\n1. Bring the stack up: `docker compose up --build` (or the local-dev flow in README.md).\n2. Add `127.0.0.1  keycloak` to your hosts file (see README.md \"One-time setup\") - required for Keycloak's issued-token issuer claim to match what the gateway validates against.\n3. Run folder '1. Infrastructure Health' to confirm everything is up.\n4. Run both requests in folder '2. Auth (Keycloak)' to populate {{adminToken}} / {{customerToken}}.\n5. Run folder '3. Product Service', then '4. Inventory Service' (to seed stock for {{sku}}), then '5. Order Service', then '6. Notification Service' - roughly the order the README's own \"Trying the API end-to-end\" walkthrough follows.\n\nAll tokens and IDs captured along the way (adminToken, customerToken, productId, orderNumber) are stored as collection variables by each request's Tests script, so requests later in the collection don't need any manual copy-pasting between them.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
